{"kind":"request","text":"Make the client `Form` transport-neutral: move the MCP act envelope to `packages/mcp` and give the MCP field checker one owner.\n\nFiled 2026-11-11 19:49 EST from a design review with Hugh. Every fact below is read at main `df41e599`. This request asks the planner to place the work in the stable-base order (`fc7576f8`). It removes a public client export, so it lands before the base freezes or it does not land.\n\n## The problem\n\n1. `formFor` in `packages/client/src/forms.ts` returns `inputSchema`. That value comes from `actInputSchema` in `packages/client/src/describe.ts`, and it is the MCP tool envelope: `target`, `idempotencyKey`, `resubmit`, `at`, `fields`, `texts`, `presented` and `values`. Its one production caller is `actTool` in `packages/mcp/src/catalogue.ts`. `FormContext.target` is MCP's rule for a singleton binding.\n2. The schema does not describe the client's own typed entry point. `handle.intents.\u003ckind\u003e` takes `AskedOf\u003cD, K\u003e`: `on`, `fields`, `presented` and `expected`. It has no `target` and no `idempotencyKey`. A handle has already bound its scope, so the target is an argument only for a surface that fronts many scopes.\n3. Three functions check a value against a `FieldType`: `fitsFieldType` in `packages/bytes/src/field-value.ts` (kernel), `shaped` in `packages/client/src/declared.ts`, and `shaped` in `packages/mcp/src/shape.ts`. The copies have drifted:\n   - The kernel and the client refuse `-0`. The MCP copy accepts it, and canonical encoding throws `CanonicalError` later, with no field path.\n   - The MCP copy, `typeWords` and `schemaOf` take `FieldLike`, an untyped record, and each has a `default:` branch. A new `FieldType` case compiles unchanged, and MCP signs a value of that type unchecked.\n   - The Git object ID pattern appears three times. MCP inlines its own `isLocalId`.\n4. Nothing ties a schema to its checker. `schemaOf` gives `time` as `format: \"date-time\"`, which admits offsets. `timeMs` accepts one UTC form that ends in `Z`. A host that validates by schema passes a value that the server refuses.\n5. Three places build a form from the same declared parts: `formFor`, the act listing at `packages/mcp/src/service.ts:1768`, and `actsOn` in `apps/room/page/src/data.ts`.\n\n## The work\n\nOne head, three parts.\n\n1. Move `actInputSchema`, `AT_INPUT`, `presentedSchema` and `schemaOf` from `packages/client/src/describe.ts` to `packages/mcp`, beside `shape.ts`. MCP is their only consumer.\n2. Remove `inputSchema` from `Form` and `target` from `FormContext`. Add the declared `presents` and the `besideOf` flags to `Form`. `Form` then holds only what the definition declares, plus the shared words. This part revises the `formFor` contract in ruling `0be8be71`.\n3. Delete the per-type `switch` in `packages/mcp/src/shape.ts`. MCP forwards to the client's checker, as `effectiveFields` already does since `d5fa31c9`. The client's checker gains three options: a member lookup for `@handle`, a text given by its digest, and a pass for a platform mark. It reports a fault code with the field path. MCP keeps its present wording in a table keyed by fault code.\n\n## Rulings the planner owes with the schedule\n\n- **`time` schema.** State the one accepted form in the schema, or leave `format: \"date-time\"`. A fix changes two places in `docs/mcp-tools.json`.\n- **`-0`.** After part 3, MCP refuses `-0` at the field path. Confirm that this visible change is wanted.\n\n## Not in this request\n\n`fitsFieldType`, `mostBytes`, `fieldAssignable`, the two parsers of a declared type (`packages/derive/src/validate/fields.ts` and `packages/platform/src/application-codec/application-projection.ts`), and the room page's `Offered` builder all stay as they are. The typed fold over field types is the follow-up request.\n\n## What to weigh\n\n- **Breaking change.** `Form`, `FormContext`, `AT_INPUT` and two members of `descriptionsOf` change in `@generalbusiness/dap-client`. The stable base is the last cheap moment.\n- **Collision.** The head edits `packages/mcp` while S4 is with the builder. Order it after S4 and after the cutover head.\n- **Kernel.** No kernel file changes and no record form is added, so the kernel filing gate does not hold it.\n- **Deployment.** The hosted MCP Workers carry the change. `MCP_ENABLED` stays off until S4 lands.\n- **Size.** An estimate from reading, not a measurement: about 55 lines leave `shape.ts`, about 80 lines move from `describe.ts`, and the fault table is the careful part.\n- **Later use.** A neutral `Form` is what a foldkit Command, a page form and an MCP tool each extend with their own envelope.","body":{"conditions":"Form has no inputSchema and FormContext has no target; packages/client holds no MCP envelope schema; packages/mcp/src/shape.ts has no per-type switch and forwards to the client's checker; MCP refusal wording is unchanged; the existing test that compares docs/mcp-tools.json passes with no change beyond a ruled time schema; npm run gate passes.","target_head":"df41e59964f09ce1d723ce870f5e4e5c6d8d4641","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}